§ `Before 1 January 2019: month and midnight by inference, everything else refuses`

#ASSERT (`the Schedule's definition of` "month" `in the text` `text inferred`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT (`the Schedule's definition of` "midnight" `in the text` `text inferred`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT (`the Schedule's definition of` "month" `in the text` `text inferred`)'s definition's `the Schedule's words` EQUALS "shall mean a calendar month"
#ASSERT (`the Schedule's definition of` "month" `in the text` `text V1`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Schedule's definition of` "person" `in the text` `text inferred`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Schedule's definition of` "act" `in the text` `text inferred`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Schedule's definition of` "act" `in the text` `text none`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Schedule's definition of` "month" `in the text` `text none`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019); and before 28 March 2003 the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation do not date the Schedule definitions of month and midnight either (L.16/2003 inserted the Schedule on that day)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Schedule's definition of` "midnight" `in the text` `text none`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019); and before 28 March 2003 the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation do not date the Schedule definitions of month and midnight either (L.16/2003 inserted the Schedule on that day)"

§ `What a definition does for a thing`

§§ `"means": a thing outside the list is outside the word`

#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "advocate" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "advocate" `text V1` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "Jersey" `text V2f` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "month" `text V2c` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`

§§ `"includes": a thing outside the list may still be within the word`

#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "land" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "land" `text V1` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "person" `text V2f` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "child" `text V2e` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`

§§ `Both (Magistrate), fork I6`

#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "Magistrate" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "Magistrate" `text V1` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "Magistrate" `text V1` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things do not exhaust the word` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "Magistrate" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things do not exhaust the word` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`

§§ `A definition that states a condition applies only where it is met`

-- "midnight, in relation to a day": the word used of a thing that is not a day is not defined by the Schedule.
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "midnight" `text V1` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `the definition does not apply: the condition it states is not met`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "midnight" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
-- "affidavit ... in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing".
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "affidavit" `text V1` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `the definition does not apply: the condition it states is not met`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "affidavit" `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "oath" `text V2d` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `the definition does not apply: the condition it states is not met`
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "swear" `text V2d` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
-- A definition with no condition ignores the flag.
#ASSERT `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "land" `text V1` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`

§§ `Unless the contrary intention appears (Article 4(1))`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "person" `text V1` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the named things are all that the word covers`
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 4(1) says the definitions in Part 1 of the Schedule apply unless the contrary intention appears, and does not say what the word then means"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "person" `text V2f` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the named things are all that the word covers`
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 4(1) says the definitions in Part 1 of the Schedule apply unless the contrary intention appears, and does not say what the word then means"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(1): how a word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule reaches a thing` "act" `text inferred` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Part 2 is only an index (Article 4(2))`

#ASSERT `the entries of the index in Part 2 of the Schedule` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(2): the meaning of a word according to Part 2 of the Schedule` "person"
        BECAUSE "Part 2 of the Schedule has effect only as an index of definitions in other enactments which are of extended application (Article 4(2)); it never supplies a meaning"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4(2): the meaning of a word according to Part 2 of the Schedule` "Companies (Jersey) Law 1991"
        BECAUSE "Part 2 of the Schedule has effect only as an index of definitions in other enactments which are of extended application (Article 4(2)); it never supplies a meaning"

§ `Midnight`

`a moment on a clock` y mo d h mi s MEANS `Local moment` OF (YMD y mo d), h, mi, s

-- The midnight of 30 June 2023 is the last moment of 30 June: 23:59:59 on 30 June is by it, 00:00:00 on 1 July is after it.
#ASSERT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 30 23 59 59)
#ASSERT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 30 0 0 0)
#ASSERT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 29 12 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 7 1 0 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 7 1 0 0 1)
-- 23:30 UTC on 30 June 2023 is 00:30 on 1 July in Jersey (BST): by midnight on 30 June on a UTC clock, after it on a Jersey clock.  The zone is the caller's (the Law names none).
#ASSERT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 30 23 30 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 7 1 0 30 0)
-- Across the leap day: the midnight of 29 February 2024 (a leap year) is the last moment of 29 February.
#ASSERT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2024 2 29) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2024 2 29 23 59 59)
#ASSERT NOT `the moment is not after the midnight of` (YMD 2024 2 29) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2024 3 1 0 0 0)

§§ `Midnight in each text`

#ASSERT (`the thing was done by midnight on` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 30 23 59 59) `in the text` `text V1`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`the thing was done by midnight on` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 6 30 23 59 59) `in the text` `text V1`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing was done by midnight on` (YMD 2023 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2023 7 1 0 0 0) `in the text` `text V2f`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`the thing was done by midnight on` (YMD 2010 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2010 6 30 12 0 0) `in the text` `text inferred`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the thing was done by midnight on` (YMD 2001 6 30) `being` (`a moment on a clock` 2001 6 30 12 0 0) `in the text` `text none`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019); and before 28 March 2003 the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation do not date the Schedule definitions of month and midnight either (L.16/2003 inserted the Schedule on that day)"

§ `A calendar month`

-- The Schedule says a month is a calendar month and nothing about adding one to a date at a month end: 31 January plus one month is not given.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day one calendar month after` (YMD 2023 1 31)
        BECAUSE "the Schedule defines a month as a calendar month and the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say how a calendar month is added to a date, or what happens at the end of a month"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day one calendar month after` (YMD 2024 2 29)
        BECAUSE "the Schedule defines a month as a calendar month and the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say how a calendar month is added to a date, or what happens at the end of a month"
